@startuml protocol-boundaries
title Blaine — protocol boundaries
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentBackgroundColor<<proposed>> #FFF2CC

component "Conversational Client" as Conversation
component "Conversational Adapter\nACP — current example" as ACP <<implementation>>
component "Personal Agent\nsemantic interpretation" as Agent <<decision>>
component "Programmable Client /\nExternal Agent" as Program
component "Programmable Adapter\nMCP / CLI — future examples" as ProgramAdapter <<proposed>>
component "Blaine Core\nprotocol-neutral operations" as Core
component "Durable Runtime\nRestate — current implementation" as Runtime <<runtime>>

Conversation --> ACP
ACP --> Agent : transport conversation
Agent --> Core : semantic requests
Program --> ProgramAdapter
ProgramAdapter --> Core : Task operations
Core --> Runtime : durable execution operations

note bottom of ACP
  ACP is transport, not
  Personal Agent semantics.
end note

note bottom of ProgramAdapter
  Adapters translate protocols;
  they do not create another Task model.
  <<proposed>> future adapter examples.
end note

note bottom of Core
  Same core operations across protocols.
  Protocol-neutral, not protocol-free.
end note

note bottom of Runtime
  Adapter session state is not durable Task state.
end note

@enduml
